				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ragnyp2umnktcv2krif4lhvs/bafkreic4bp7eqwo24hvcmjzs4hpqt24lvd4qbhay5l3b2t5ody46gyvlyu"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-25T18:05:20.939Z",
			"content": "<p>Nice! Seeing as smol size is a prime feature of this lib, are you open to contributions that reduce the number of minified bytes at the expense of some readability?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:ragnyp2umnktcv2krif4lhvs/app.bsky.feed.post/3lusnahpe5s2q",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ragnyp2umnktcv2krif4lhvs/app.bsky.feed.post/3lusn6khu2k2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mxdvl.com/post/3lusnahpe5s2q",
			"author": {
				"name": "Max Duval",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mxdvl.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ragnyp2umnktcv2krif4lhvs/bafkreic4bp7eqwo24hvcmjzs4hpqt24lvd4qbhay5l3b2t5ody46gyvlyu"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-25T18:06:25.148Z",
			"content": "<p>And how important is it that errors are specific, for example regarding fractional hours &amp; minutes? I can see the test don’t currently capture that distinction.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lusnem65r22p",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ragnyp2umnktcv2krif4lhvs/app.bsky.feed.post/3lusnahpe5s2q",
